      "data": {
        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory.\n\nHere are the files and their purposes:\n\n**Same-scenario scored files:**\n1. `summarize_text.py` - Calls a hosted LLM to summarize long text.\n2. `extract_json.py` - Calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text.\n3. `answer_with_context.py` - Calls a hosted LLM to answer a question using provided context.\n4. `stream_completion.py` - Streams partial output tokens from a hosted LLM.\n\n**Local helper files:**\n5. `model_client.py` - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection.\n6. `model_models.py` - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection.\n\n**Later-step scored files:**\n7. `prompt_safety.py` - Checks prompts and generated text for unsafe content.\n8. `result_translate.py` - Translates generated model output.\n9. `output_embedding.py` - Embeds model outputs for clustering or retrieval.\n10. `spoken_brief.py` - Generates a spoken brief from the model output.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Microsoft/OpenAI as the concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
